nt/system property is needed — Fast Infoset is pure in-memory binary XML (de)serialization, with no external service, matching the plain JVM unit-test style already used for `rt`, `jaxws-rt`, and `FastInfoset` in this repo.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"rt-fi is a thin optional Fast Infoset codec plug-in for the JAX-WS RI core runtime; its codec classes implement rt's StreamSOAPCodec/Packet-based API, so meaningful tests need com.sun.xml.ws:rt directly on the test classpath (rt-fi is meant to sit alongside an rt/jaxws-rt install, the classic 'provided scope' bridge-module pattern). No Docker image or system property is needed - FastInfoset is pure in-memory binary XML encoding.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n      \"coordinate\": \"com.sun.xml.ws:rt:4.0.5\",\n      \"scope\": \"testImplementation\",\n      \"reason\": \"rt-fi's codec classes (e.g. FastInfosetStreamSOAPCodec) implement interfaces and use types (Packet, SOAPVersion, StreamSOAPCodec) declared in com.sun.xml.ws:rt. rt-fi is an optional runtime add-on meant to sit alongside an existing rt/jaxws-rt installation, so its POM likely depends on rt with 'provided' scope, which Gradle does not resolve transitively for a standalone testImplementation on rt-fi.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Test FastInfosetCodec/FastInfosetStreamSOAPCodec directly at the unit level (build a Packet/SOAP message, encode it, assert the output is Fast Infoset binary - e.g. starts with the FI magic byte 0xE0 - then decode it back) rather than attempting end-to-end HTTP content negotiation. This matches the existing unit-test style already used for the sibling com.sun.xml.ws:rt and com.sun.xml.ws:jaxws-rt artifacts in this repo and avoids needing a servlet container or Docker image. No environment variables or system properties are required.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"This sandboxed environment has no network access, so the rt-fi POM's actual